  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Securing Rights for Women and Girls in Karonga</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Outcomes
1.	Reduced incidence of cases of violence against women and girls in two traditional authorities in Karonga Diocese.
2.	Women have increased access to justice delivery systems in the targeted areas 

Activities
1.1.Conduct 1 training and sensitisation meeting with religious and traditional leaders in women&#x2019;s rights, social justice, inheritance law,

1.2.Hold 2 monitoring and review meetings (every 6 months) with traditional and religious leaders, to discuss gender-related issues in their communities,

1.3.Hold  2 training workshops for  parish justice and peace committees in women&#x2019;s rights, social justice, gender based violence, case recording and investigation skills, Catholic social Teaching and spirituality of justice,
2.1.Train 40 members of 2 parish justice and peace teams in basic paralegal skills,

2.2.Each trained paralegal will conduct at least 2 community awareness meetings per quarter, with each  meeting targeting at least 20 participants.

2.3.Establish links and relationships with formal and informal justice delivery systems in the target areas,

2.4.Trained paralegals refer women and girls to service providers,

2.5.Hold quarterly monitoring, review and support meetings for parish justice and peace teams,</narrative>
  </description>
